<BaseLayout title="Privacy Policy | Web Grouth" description="How Web Grouth handles information shared through this website."><section class="legal"><div class="narrow"><div class="eyebrow"><span class="eyebrow-dot"></span> Legal</div><h1>Privacy Policy</h1><p>Last updated: August 30, 2026</p><h2>Information you share</h2><p>When you contact Web Grouth, you may provide your name, email address, website, campaign requirements and other information needed to respond to your request.</p><h2>How information is used</h2><p>We use the information you provide to answer enquiries, prepare relevant service options, communicate about active work and improve our services. We do not sell your personal information.</p><h2>Third-party communication</h2><p>If you choose to continue through WhatsApp or email, those services process your information under their own privacy terms. The website form prepares a WhatsApp message for your review and does not send it automatically.</p><h2>Data retention</h2><p>Business correspondence may be retained for as long as reasonably necessary to manage enquiries, deliver services and maintain appropriate records.</p><h2>Your choices</h2><p>You may ask us to correct or delete personal information held in our direct business records, subject to any legal or operational record-keeping requirements.</p><h2>Contact</h2><p>For privacy questions, email <a class="text-link" href="mailto:contact@webgrouth.com">contact@webgrouth.com <span>↗</span></a>.</p></div></section></BaseLayout>
